---
const capabilities = [
  { title: 'AI tooling', body: 'Building doc pipelines with RAG, MCP agents, and constraint-bound generation.' },
  { title: 'Information architecture', body: 'Structuring large content systems so everything is findable and nothing is duplicated.' },
  { title: 'Docs-as-code', body: 'Docs that live in version control, ship with CI/CD, and review like software.' },
  { title: 'Technical writing', body: 'Developer-grade clarity for API references, SDKs, guides, and release notes.' },
  { title: 'Agentic systems', body: 'Designing multi-step AI workflows that produce consistent, auditable output at scale.' },
  { title: 'Content strategy', body: 'Content audits, taxonomy design, and doc-site IA for complex product surfaces.' },
];
---

<section id="about" class="cds-section cds-rule-top">
  <div class="cds-container">
    <div class="about">
      <div class="about__sticky">
        <p class="type-label" data-reveal>About</p>
        <h2 class="type-h2" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="60">I make complicated platforms make sense.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="about__body">
        <div class="about__narrative" data-reveal>
          <p>I started writing developer documentation in 2008 and have spent most of the years since on the hard cases: inference SDKs, enterprise CX platforms, structured authoring systems, and internal tools that never had a doc team before I showed up.</p>
          <p>At Salesforce I spent two years designing AI-assisted workflows for a documentation team. Not automation for its own sake. Targeted tools that removed the parts of the job that grind writers down, so the editorial judgment they're actually good at could go further and faster.</p>
          <p>I work in the stack now, not just the editor. Git, Python, CI/CD, agent frameworks. That lets me build systems that fit how engineering teams actually ship.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cap" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="60">
          {capabilities.map(c => (
            <div class="cap__item">
              <div class="cap__title"><span class="cap__dot"></span>{c.title}</div>
              <p class="cap__body">{c.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--sp-08); }
  @media (min-width: 1056px) { .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr; gap: var(--sp-10); } }
  .about__sticky .type-h2 { margin-top: var(--sp-04); }
  @media (min-width: 1056px) { .about__sticky { position: sticky; top: 96px; } }

  .about__narrative p { font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.3vw, 1.125rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--cds-text-secondary); margin: 0 0 var(--sp-05); }
  .about__narrative { margin-bottom: var(--sp-08); }

  .cap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; border-top: 1px solid var(--cds-border-subtle); }
  @media (min-width: 672px) { .cap { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .cap__item { padding: var(--sp-05) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cds-border-subtle); }
  @media (min-width: 672px) { .cap__item:nth-child(odd) { padding-right: var(--sp-07); border-right: 1px solid var(--cds-border-subtle); } .cap__item:nth-child(even) { padding-left: var(--sp-07); } }
  .cap__title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-03); font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--cds-text-primary); margin-bottom: var(--sp-03); }
  .cap__dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; background: var(--cds-link-primary); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .cap__body { font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--cds-text-helper); margin: 0; }
</style>
